==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|lecherous|lang=enm}}, {{term|licherous|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term/t|fro|*lecherous}} (attested in {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|lecherousement||lecherously|lang=fro}}), from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|lecherie|lang=fro}}, {{term|licherie||gluttony, sensuality, lewdness, lechery|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|lecher|lang=fro}}, {{term|lechier|lang=fro}}, {{term|lekier|lang=fro}}, {{term|lescher||to lick, live in gluttony or sensuality|lang=fro}}, from Old {{etyl|frk|en}} {{term/t|frk|*lekkon|*lekkōn|to lick}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*likkōną||to lick}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-||to lick}}, equivalent to {{suffix|lecher|ous}}. More at {{l|en|lick}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# given to excessive sexual activity and [[debauchery]]

